							Step 1: Inspect Your Skirt Construction & Underlayers
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
							Look at the bottom hem of your gown. If it is a clean fabric edge (crepe, mikado, or satin), select <strong>Plain Clean Hem ($140)</strong>. If the edge features a stiff nylon ribbon that keeps the skirt flared, select <strong>Horsehair Braid ($210)</strong>. If it has intricate lace patterns along the perimeter, select <strong>Scalloped Lace Border ($320)</strong>. Next, lift the outer skirt and count how many layers of crinoline, tulle, or lining are underneath—enter this number into <strong>Extra Skirt Underlayers</strong> so each layer is accurately accounted for.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem;">
						<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--accent-blue); margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
							Step 2: Check Your Bodice Fit & Undergarment Needs
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
							Try on your dress with your intended bridal undergarments. If the waist or bust is loose or tight, check <strong>Take In / Let Out Bodice ($120)</strong>. If you want built-in bust support so you don't need a strapless bra, check <strong>Sew-In Molded Bra Cups ($40)</strong>. If the straps slip off your shoulders, check <strong>Shorten Straps / Sleeves ($50)</strong>.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div style="background: var(--bg-paper); border: 2px solid var(--fg-pencil); border-radius: 6px; padding: 1.25rem;">
						<h4 class="font-heading" style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #16a34a; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
							Step 3: Choose Your Train Bustle Style
						</h4>
						<p class="font-body" style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
							If your gown has a train, you will need a bustle to secure the fabric off the floor during your reception dance. A <strong>1-Point American Bustle ($75)</strong> works great for short sweep trains. For heavier cathedral trains or mermaid gowns, select a <strong>3 to 5-Point French Bustle ($135)</strong> for balanced weight distribution.
						</p>
