					</summary>
					<p class="font-body" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-blue); font-size: 1.05rem;">
						Standard wedding dresses have very limited seam allowances (usually 0.5 to 1 inch max). While taking a dress in by 1 to 2 sizes is routine, letting a dress out is difficult. If extra space is required, the best solution is converting a zipper back into a corset lace-up back, which instantly adds 1 to 2 inches of room.
