						The hemline of a wedding gown must graze exactly 1 inch above the floor so you don't trip while walking down the aisle. A 2-inch heel vs. a 3.5-inch heel completely changes the hemline measurement. If you change your shoes after your hem is cut, you will either trip or your shoes will show in photos.
					</p>
